@EstatePulse_HostAddress = http://localhost:5295

### 1. Get all users
GET {{EstatePulse_HostAddress}}/api/users
Accept: application/json

### 2. Get all users with query filter
GET {{EstatePulse_HostAddress}}/api/users?search=john&role=Customer&isActive=true
Accept: application/json

### 3. Create a new user (JSON)
POST {{EstatePulse_HostAddress}}/api/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "John Doe",
  "email": "john.doe@example.com",
  "phoneNumber": "+1234567890",
  "password": "Password123!",
  "role": "Customer",
  "nationalIdCard": "ID123456",
  "avatarUrl": "https://example.com/avatar.png"
}

### 4. Get user by ID
GET {{EstatePulse_HostAddress}}/api/users/1
Accept: application/json

### 5. Update user (JSON)
PUT {{EstatePulse_HostAddress}}/api/users/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "John Updated",
  "email": "john.doe@example.com",
  "phoneNumber": "+1987654321",
  "password": "NewSecurePassword123!",
  "role": "Agent",
  "nationalIdCard": "ID987654",
  "isActive": true,
  "avatarUrl": "https://example.com/new-avatar.png"
}

### 6. Delete user by ID
DELETE {{EstatePulse_HostAddress}}/api/users/1
